Cases:
- Compose preflight and config --services: PASS; services postgres, migrate, backend, frontend resolved; named volume brewlite_pgdata resolved.
- `docker compose -p scrum94p2d2e1 ... up --build -d` expected all services to reach health; actual exit 1. The frontend image, backend image and migrate image built. PostgreSQL became healthy. Migrate exited 0 after applying 9/9 migrations against database brewlite_compose at postgres:5432. Backend restarted unhealthy and the frontend remained Created because the backend dependency never became healthy.
- Backend startup log: `Missing required environment variable: VNPAY_TMN_CODE` from the production reconciliation QueryDR configuration. This is a missing local Sandbox configuration precondition; it does not establish a code defect.
